==============================================================================
O17 — disjoint-block residual  (fit-free; exact counts; projection, not fit)
==============================================================================
  x_j  = x0 * r^j                        value ladder
  c_j  = pi(x_{j+1}) - pi(x_j)           EXACT integer count in (x_j, x_{j+1}]
  L_j  = li(x_{j+1}) - li(x_j)           smooth prediction
  e_j  = c_j - L_j                       the residual
  ehat = e_j / sqrt(x_j)                 half-power normalisation

  Blocks are DISJOINT and TILE the range: every prime in (x_0, x_last] is used
  exactly once and every block is an independent sample. The COUNT fluctuates,
  because the interval is fixed in VALUE space, not in index space.
  O12-O15 summed primes[N:2N] by PRIME INDEX: consecutive rungs overlapped, and
  the count was fixed at N by construction, so it carried no fluctuation at all.

  log-x step = log(r) = 0.6931472   (dyadic ladder: log 2 = 0.6931472)
  Nyquist = pi/log(r) = 4.532360   (dyadic ladder: 4.532360)
